sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Institutional User
    participant Frontend as Next.js 15 Client (/login)
    participant NextAuth as NextAuth.js v5 (Auth.js)
    participant Backend as FastAPI Auth Router (/api/v1/auth)
    participant DB as Database (User Table)
    participant ProtectedAPI as Protected Endpoint (/api/v1/platform/*)

    alt Password Credentials Login
        User->>Frontend: Submit Email & Password
        Frontend->>NextAuth: signIn("credentials", { email, password })
        NextAuth->>DB: Query User Record & Verify BCrypt Hash (cost factor 12)
        Note over NextAuth: Gated Prisma adapter ensures fallback in air-gapped dev
        NextAuth-->>Frontend: Set authjs.session-token Cookie (JWT)
        Frontend->>Backend: POST /api/v1/auth/login
        Backend->>DB: Verify BCrypt Hash
        Backend-->>Frontend: Return FastAPI Access Token (JWT with Role & Permissions)
    else Google SSO OAuth 2.0 Login
        User->>Frontend: Click "Sign in with Google"
        Frontend->>NextAuth: signIn("google")
        NextAuth->>User: Redirect to Google Accounts OAuth 2.0
        User->>NextAuth: Authorize & Return Auth Code
        NextAuth->>DB: Upsert User & Account Record
        NextAuth-->>Frontend: Set authjs.session-token Cookie
    end

    User->>Frontend: Navigate to Protected Route (/dashboard, /agent-console)
    Frontend->>ProtectedAPI: Request with Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
    ProtectedAPI->>Backend: set_user_context() Dependency
    Backend->>Backend: Verify JWT Signature (HMAC SHA-256)
    Backend->>Backend: Inspect Roles & Permissions via require_permission()
    Note over Backend: RFC 7662 Token Introspection validates scopes
    Backend-->>Frontend: Return Protected Institutional Analytics Data
